docs/catalog-sources/group3-hoist-arsenal-prime-atlantis-rogue-impulse-legend-sorinex-titan.md:52:Naming caveat (important): Hoist has TWO generations of ROC-IT selectorized SKUs in the wild. The current site lists RS-2xxx. Dealer catalogues (Portland Fitness Equipment, BGI Fitness, Fitness Equipment Specialists, National Gym Supply/gympart.com) list the earlier RS-1xxx equivalents, e.g. **RS-1301 Chest Press** — verified as a real, separately-cataloged model, not a typo for RS-2301. Note that RS-1502 Lateral Raise and RS-1103 Triceps Extension still appear on Hoist's own current collection page, so the two number families coexist. If a user is standing in front of an older Hoist ROC-IT, the sticker may read RS-1xxx. Only RS-1301, RS-1502 and RS-1103 are confirmed here by direct sighting; do NOT auto-generate the rest of the RS-1xxx family.
docs/catalog-sources/group3-hoist-arsenal-prime-atlantis-rogue-impulse-legend-sorinex-titan.md:152:Notes: Hoist SKUs are highly reliable because their own Shopify collections publish them. The one real risk is the RS-1xxx vs RS-2xxx generation split described above — treat them as distinct catalog entries rather than merging them. The HF-series add-on benches (e.g. HF-5165 7 Position F.I.D. Bench, HF-4263-MB Ab/Back Hyper Bench, HF-4145-PL Folding Multi Bench) appeared in a search snippet of Hoist's HF Add Ons collection but I did not load that collection page directly, so treat those three as lower confidence.
docs/catalog-sources/group3-hoist-arsenal-prime-atlantis-rogue-impulse-legend-sorinex-titan.md:714:- **Hoist Fitness** — all lines read directly off hoistfitness.com collection pages: ROC-IT Selectorized (21), ROC-IT Plate Loaded (13), HD Dual Series (11 stations), Club Line (14), Commercial Freeweights (24), Multi-Jungle (6), MotionCage (10), plus home lines. Only caveat is the RS-1xxx/RS-2xxx generation split.
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:3:Manufacturers: Life Fitness, Hammer Strength, Precor, Cybex, Nautilus, Star Trac, Body-Solid.
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:548:## Star Trac
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:552:- https://www.strengthindustry.com/star-trac (dealer catalogue — used for Star Trac-branded strength names)
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:554:**Important finding, please read before seeding.** Star Trac's current manufacturer catalog (corehandf.com) is **cardio only** — 10 Series, 8 Series, 6 Series, 4 Series, S Series, Virtual Bike. Star Trac and Nautilus are both Core Health & Fitness brands, and the strength lines that were once sold as Star Trac (**Impact**, **Inspiration**, **Instinct**, **Leverage**) are today catalogued and sold under the **Nautilus** brand — the machines listed in the Nautilus section above are the same machines. The "Star Trac Instinct" trademark was cancelled in 2019.
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:556:### Star Trac-branded strength — verified individual names
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:557:Only these Star Trac-branded strength model names were actually seen in a catalogue listing:
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:558:- Star Trac Impact Seated Leg Press — leg press (selectorized)
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:559:- Star Trac Inspiration Abduction/Adduction Combo — leg abduction + adduction (selectorized) **MULTI**
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:560:- Star Trac Inspiration Glute Press — glute press / hip extension (selectorized)
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:561:- Star Trac Instinct Leg Curl — leg curl (selectorized)
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:562:- Star Trac Leverage Lat Pulldown — lat pulldown (plate-loaded)
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:563:- Star Trac Instinct Circuit — multi-machine circuit package **MULTI**
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:564:- Star Trac Instinct Smith Machine — Smith machine (`smith/rack`)
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:565:- Star Trac Instinct DAP Functional Trainer — cable crossover / functional trainer (`cable`) **MULTI**
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:567:### Product LINES identified but not enumerable under the Star Trac brand
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:568:Impact Strength · Inspiration · Instinct · Leverage · Legacy (the older Star Trac strength line Impact Strength is described by Core as "based on the popular feel of their Legacy strength line").
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:571:- **I deliberately did not generate a full Star Trac machine list by copying the Nautilus lists and swapping the brand name.** That is exactly the extrapolation this task forbids. If you want Star Trac coverage in the app, the safest treatment is a single "Star Trac (Impact / Inspiration / Instinct / Leverage)" grouping that maps onto the Nautilus models, or brand-agnostic entries — because a member standing in front of an "Instinct Leg Curl" may be looking at either a Star Trac or a Nautilus badge depending on the manufacturing year.
docs/catalog-sources/group1-lifefitness-hammerstrength-precor-cybex-nautilus-startrac-bodysolid.md:678:- **Star Trac strength.** Star Trac's current manufacturer catalog is cardio only. Its strength lines now ship as Nautilus. I verified only 8 Star Trac-branded strength model names, all from dealer listings, and I refused to reconstruct the line by rebranding the Nautilus lists. Read the Star Trac section's note before you seed anything for this brand.
