Notes:
- **Signature Series selectorized is DISCONTINUED.** The Life Fitness catalog page for "Signature Series Chest Press" explicitly says the product is discontinued and names "Insignia Series Dual Axis Chest Press" as its replacement. Signature Series machines are still extremely common in real gyms, so they belong in the catalog — but I could only verify these individual Signature Series names from live Life Fitness page titles: **Signature Series Chest Press, Signature Series Row, Signature Series Pulldown, Signature Series Leg Extension, Signature Series Dual Adjustable Pulley, Signature Series Adjustable Cable Crossover, Signature Series Multi-Jungle MJ8, Signature Series Olympic Squat Rack, Signature Series Plate Loaded Leg Extension, Signature Series Plate Loaded Linear Leg Press.** A dealer page listed a typical Signature Series circuit as including shoulder press, pec fly, lat pulldown, row rear delt, biceps curl, triceps, leg curl, hip adductor, abductor and abdominal — I did **not** verify those as exact Life Fitness model names and have deliberately not listed them.
- The Insignia catalog page's own header claimed "30" machines while enumerating 27; the shop collection claimed 29. I list 28 (the 27 enumerated + Insignia Series Seated Leg Press, verified separately from its own catalog page). There are likely 1–2 Insignia pieces I did not see. Do not guess them.
- "Circuit Series" exists as a Life Fitness line but its pages return "Product Discontinued" (e.g. Circuit Series Leg Extension). I did not enumerate it.

