Catalog audit so far: the 12 legacy exercise IDs/names and 24 legacy model IDs/manufacturer/name triples match the base catalog exactly after sorting by UUID. The advertised duplicate guard is weaker: it catches exact strings only, and the expanded catalog contains confirmed same-product aliases with different UUIDs. I’m validating those against the committed research and checking tests/migrations before grading the tickets.
